# 2.3.scenario.enumeration.blend.stone

## .what

merge the two candidate sets — imagination + literature — into **one lineup**, with each scenario's
source stream marked. the disagreement between streams is itself signal.

## .inputs

- `2.1.scenario.enumeration.from.imagination.yield.md`
- `2.2.scenario.enumeration.from.literature.yield.md`

## .do

- union the two sets into one deduplicated scenario list
- tag each scenario's provenance: imagination-only · literature-only · both
- flag **imagination-only** scenarios as "plausible but unattested" — they carry no literature
  weight, so they will lean hard on the assay (they survive on severity, per superposition-until-elimination)
- flag **literature-only** scenarios as a logic blind-spot worth a second look

## .emit

into `2.3.scenario.enumeration.blend.yield.md` — the single sourced lineup.

## .done when

one deduplicated lineup exists, each scenario provenance-tagged, imagination-only + literature-only
branches flagged.
